# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That caused three problems:
#   - Biome's formatter reported every source file as unformatted.
#   - Astro's asset hash for src/assets/*.svg did not match the deployed
#     build, because the hashed content differed by line endings.
#   - public/robots.txt shipped with CRLF instead of LF.
#   - src/content/blog/*.md CRLF could render as stray characters.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` forces LF in the
# working tree on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# These are binary. Never apply line-ending conversion or text diffing.
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary

# Keep lockfiles diffable but normalized like everything else.
bun.lock text eol=lf
